-- Phase 3 scoring, generated by drizzle-kit:
--
-- scores_type_ck gains `text_match`, the eighth scorer type (SCORER_TYPES;
-- plan 9.3, DESIGN_CHECKS_FIX_PROMPT.md Part F). A CHECK change fires no row
-- trigger, and existing rows hold only the seven older types.
--
-- Nothing else needs DDL. Re-score (plan 9.4) runs through the 0001 triggers
-- unchanged, which phase3-migration.spec.ts checks step by step:
--   * the new generation's insert: evaluations_require_executed (the run's
--     current attempt is executed), evaluations_in_flight_uq (one queued or
--     running evaluation per run, so double clicks collapse), and the publish
--     guard's insert rule (it starts queued);
--   * claim and claim renewal: only claim_token and claim_expires_at move on
--     a running evaluation, which evaluations_guard allows;
--   * publish: the previous result is superseded while the new one runs (the
--     publish guard wants a newer running or completed generation), then the
--     new one completes with exactly the task's keys for the same attempt;
--     the run stays `scored`, and evaluations_results_revision raises the
--     experiment's results revision;
--   * the dead letter for a re-score: `failed` is allowed because the run has
--     a current result, which stays current.
-- The judge's tokens and cost live in scores.evidence (jsonb, no CHECK), and
-- the new `network` fields of the timeline are a view, not a column.

